KZ3 patch 1097 (SPU pass 72): cheaper SPU job code and direct hops for the audio mixer jobs.

- fsmb/fsmbi: one 16-entry nibble table per SPU word (a constant immediate folds to a constant vector); the byte
  loop was not unrolled by GCC -O2 (3.4 % of the audio synth job, SPU pass 71).
- cbd/chd/cwd/cdd (and the x forms): the generate-controls as tables (16/8/4/2 entries) instead of a 16-byte loop
  per call (spu_cwd_pos 4.5 % of the job).
- cflts/cfltu/csflt/cuflt: four lanes in SSE4.1 double arithmetic instead of a scalar loop (same operations: widen,
  scale by the power of two, clamp, truncate; cfltu converts floor(v) - 2^31 and flips the top bit). NaN lanes give
  the loops' values (operand order of min/max); the loops stay for builds without SSE4.1; exp2 replaced by the
  power of two from its exponent bits.
- fma/fms/fnms: a lane whose double sum sits on a float rounding midpoint no longer goes to the per-lane libm
  path when the double sum is exact (TwoSum error 0): then it is the fused value and its rounding to float is the
  correctly rounded result. K2 (SPU pass 72, KZ3_SPU_FMASTATS=1): 158 M midpoint fallback lanes, the most common
  reason (products of short mantissas).
- fma/fms/fnms with -mfma (KZ3_SPU_ISA): one hardware fused multiply-add per vector; a lane whose result has
  exponent 0 (non-zero), 1 or 255 sends the vector through the double path unchanged, so the bits are the same
  (FTZ mode, the default); the -mfma build used the scalar per-lane path before (no FTZ).
- direct hops (patch 1096): a computed hop to the innermost bracket's return pc returns to the host caller with
  nothing pending (the drain only returned there, before any hook; the inline spu_drain_call then takes its fast
  path); spu_ib_direct filters the taskset tests by bitmaps (policy image ids, hashed task entries) before the LS
  read and the table scans, and probes the spu_lookup memo inline.
Every helper change is bit-identical to the old code (tools/spu/test_spu_cg72.sh); hops: tools/spu/test_spu_hop.sh.
Upstream candidate (helpers, the hop return).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

